{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1476711-homebrew-rubber-band-society","id":1476711,"title":"[Homebrew] Rubber Band Society","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-03-19T00:28:07-07:00","id":1476711,"title":"[Homebrew] Rubber Band Society","content":"<i>&quot;Think of the rubber band as a metaphor for existence: we all have enormous potential for creation and destruction, ready to be actualized at any moment, but without inherent guidance. To understand the true meaning of both Gnosis and Wisdom, you must learn how to release that potential in every bruise and brushstroke, every scream and poem, every concussion and orgasm. If no sensation of life or death is alien to you, no situation can compromise your Understanding nor tempt you with Hubris. Be flexible and know when to release.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Purpose:</b> The pursuit of enlightenment and fulfillment through synergy between martial sublimation and artistic catharsis.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Relic:</b> A collection of rubber band balls, with each band being made of Perfected Rubber and representing a cultist who managed to Awaken while following this Mystery Cult's Purpose. There are 10 such Relics, with one for each Path and one for each Order, and they </span>can be used as +2 Tool Yantras for any spell related to the purview of this Mystery Cult.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Doctrine:</b> A combination of the ideologies of the Adamantine Arrow and the Free Council, mainly the precept of seeking challenges and the belief of inherent magical potential within Sleeper Traditions.<br /> <br /> <b>Common Legacies:</b> Universal Harmony, Uncrowned Kings, Perfected Adepts, Bearers Of The Sigil, Danse Diabolique, Pygmalian Society.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Initiation Benefits</span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u25cf - A Specialty for Crafts or Expression reflecting something like Sculptures or Paintings. Alternatively, a Specialty in Brawl or Weaponry reflecting something like Boxing or Shivs. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u25cf\u25cf - Contacts (Artists or Fighters). </span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf - +1 Crafts, Expression, Brawl or Weaponry.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf - Biokinesis 3 or Psychometry. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf - Access to 3 dots in an Influence related to combat or art, which can be activated via Willpower instead of Essence on a 1 for 1 ratio. Their dice pool is based on the type of Influence, but it defaults to [Strength + Brawl Or Weaponry] or [Intelligence + Crafts Or Expression]. They may also acquire Merits that enhance or alter their Influences by making Pacts and learning Thaumaturgy, as detailed in Summoners and Second Sight, respectively.</span><br /> <br /> Mages replace the benefit of the 4th level of Initiation with 3 Rotes related to combat or art. Instead of the benefit of the 5th level of Initiation, the Mage can achieve Exceptional Success with 3 Successes when he casts any spell related to combat or art, once per Chapter. This cannot be stacked with Rotes, but if stacked with a Praxis, the Mage can acquire 2 distinct benefits of Exceptional Success on spellcasting, such as Mana Refill and an Arcane Condition, but not two Arcane Conditions. Mages of the Rubber Band Society often use this benefit to acquire Persistent Arcane Conditions with advantages and disadvantages that match the purview of the Rubber Band Society. Consult this <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S5lA00oP8kKrYW76B0bRVn-vYyy5Hl6aKQFtCakVPck/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><b>list of homebrewed Persistent Arcane Conditions</b></a> for examples. Mages<span style=\"font-size:12px\"> may also pay Mana per Story to have temporary access to additional benefits within the Rubber Band Society's purview, which include but are not limited to: </span><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:12px\">An Awakened Mentor. (Mana Equal To Merit Rating X 10) </span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Artifacts and Mysteries. (5 To 25 Mana For Mysteries, Mana Equal To Merit Rating X 5 For Artifacts) </span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Grimoires, Imbued Items and Hallows. (Mana Equal To Merit Rating X 2)<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u200b</span></span></span></li> </ul><b><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Plot Hooks:</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">The Rubber Band Society used to offer a VIP audience with a Royal Avatar of any Aeon in exchange for 1000 Mana and 3 favors for its founder, Saliva. This service has been discontinued indefinitely, and their official Logogram page does not offer any details on what led to this decision, or when this service will be available again, if at all. Saliva has so far refused all requests for an interview regarding this discontinuation, and the local Guardians Of The Veil are suspecting that he is involved in Left-Handed activities.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">A Sleepwalker who has been obsessively collecting artworks and weapons associated with the Rubber Band Society has turned into a type of Proximus which was believed to have gone extinct when its last known member ventured into the Astral Realms in search of a complete Awakening and never returned. This Proximus is not interested in continuing their Dynasty via reproduction and inheritance, but via artistic inspiration and martial training. There is substantial evidence that this might be possible, if not reliable or safe.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 11-29-2022, 02:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-19T00:29:35-07:00","id":1476712,"title":"","content":"I was trying to figure out what services/products Mages can reasonably expect to acquire by using Mana as a currency, instead of only trading favors for other favors. I ended up sketching this for such purposes. The Rubber Band is inspired by the various fighters from Grappler Baki, Jhin The Virtuoso from League of Legends, Sander Cohen from Bioshock, The Phantom Of The Opera and Are We Cool Yet? from SCP Foundation. They are essentially a club for exceptionally weird and volatile Mages who are in serious need of an escape valve for their violent/artistic desires. Logogram is a social media app developed by the Free Council that I like to include in my Chronicles. It has support for High Speech, among other features mainly based on innovative applications of the Prime Arcanum.<br /> <br /> I left the details of the Rubber Band up to the reader's imagination, so they can be adjusted for specific Chronicles. That being said, if you wanna get an approximation of how I'd characterize them in general, check out <a href=\"https://youtu.be/EOnSh3QlpbQ\" target=\"_blank\"><b>this video</b></a> and <a href=\"https://youtu.be/XWuPGKLJXe8\" target=\"_blank\"><b>this video</b></a>. Saliva's main traits are: Thyrsus Libertine, Clavicularius, Virtue of Charity, Vice of Wrath, Obsessions [Biological Editing, Shamanistic Synergy, Goetic Therapy]. He is the type of Mage who sincerely believes there's nothing wrong with giving people symbionts designed to scrub harmful cholesterol from their veins, nothing wrong with implanting hypnotic dreams in a politician's mind to make them less likely to take bribes, and most definitely nothing wrong with doing it all and more while chewing cryptid-mushrooms and wrestling violence-spirits.<br /> <br /> The Rubber Band's prices are deliberately set high so PCs can use Social Maneuvering or equivalent to bargain for discounts. I have not exactly defined what category of organization the Rubber Band is meant to be, but you can think of them as an something closer to an extended pseudo-Cabal, rather than a Nameless Order or Legacy. If you have questions about these Mages, or would like to propose similar groups with their own lists of services/products, let me know and we can figure something out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 11-15-2022, 05:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-19T03:59:15-07:00","id":1476720,"title":"","content":"How can bonuses to Wisdom rolls be a service they can pay for, or bargain their way into cheaper prices?<br /> <br /> And how would that work for their per-turn mana limits?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-19T04:19:23-07:00","id":1476721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1476711-homebrew-rubber-band-society?p=1476720#post1476720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How can bonuses to Wisdom rolls be a service they can pay for, or bargain their way into cheaper prices?<br /> <br /> And how would that work for their per-turn mana limits?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking that they are a support group first and foremost, who help each other blow off steam by critiquing each other's punches and paintings. Just a bunch of Mages yelling in a friendly way at each other about color theory and chokeholds, and generally doing practical arcane exercises in controlled and safe environments to expose themselves to situations that could tempt them with Hubris. The end result, as I imagine it, is a greater understanding of the potential consequences of magic utilized in a violent or artistic context. The per-turn limits for Mana expenditure wouldn't apply, since the Rubber Band has a Disciple of Prime who casts Channel Mana to take the payment from you and convert it into packages of Tass, which is done in down-time rather than in the span of turns.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-19T08:33:49-07:00","id":1476730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1476711-homebrew-rubber-band-society?p=1476721#post1476721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking that they are a support group first and foremost, who help each other blow off steam by critiquing each other's punches and paintings. Just a bunch of Mages yelling in a friendly way at each other about color theory and chokeholds, and generally doing practical arcane exercises in controlled and safe environments to expose themselves to situations that could tempt them with Hubris. The end result, as I imagine it, is a greater understanding of the potential consequences of magic utilized in a violent or artistic context.</div> </div> </div> </div>That kind of sounds to me like something that gets a bit weird as something they have to pay for on a per-case basis, and it would make more sense as the group culture providing the definition for what even count as Acts of Hubris, which by the base rules is still supposed to be something flexible between characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-19T14:47:05-07:00","id":1476746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1476711-homebrew-rubber-band-society?p=1476730#post1476730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That kind of sounds to me like something that gets a bit weird as something they have to pay for on a per-case basis, and it would make more sense as the group culture providing the definition for what even count as Acts of Hubris, which by the base rules is still supposed to be something flexible between characters.</div> </div> </div> </div> That is a good point, making it a part of their culture makes more sense. As for Wisdom being flexible between characters, I imagine that Mages who gravitate toward the Rubber Band do so for flexible reasons. In other words, if you were a Mage who has a lot of artistic potential and difficulty with not hurting people, you'd end up risking certain Acts of Hubris sooner or later. This in turn might cause the local Guardians Of The Veil to recommend the Rubber Band to you in order to provide therapy for your issues (if only so the Guardians Of The Veil have less work to do and can focus better on that Abyssal Incursion over there). As you participate and assimilate, your understanding of Wisdom changes to accommodate various tenets of responsibility related to art and violence. In fact, I would say the Rubber Band has its equivalent of Order Doctrine (e.g. &quot;Sins For A Just End Grant Wisdom&quot; and &quot;Existence Is War&quot;). Some sort of threefold principle akin to this:<ul><li>Creation Is Given Form Through Ideas: Potential and passion mean nothing unless channeled through technique and theory.</li> <li>Ideas Must Be Subjected To Destruction: If your designs seem amazing to you tomorrow, take them apart and piece them together.</li> <li>Within Destruction, There Is Also Creation: Use what is destructive or ugly as inspiration for what is constructive or beautiful.</li> </ul>EDIT: I included the threefold principle in the original post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 03-19-2022, 06:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-13T04:55:43-07:00","id":1490014,"title":"","content":"Updated the original post. The Rubber Band Society is now explicitly a Mystery Cult under the guidance of the Free Council and Adamantine Arrow, complete with alternate benefits for Mages who invest into Mystery Cult Influence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-15T15:01:34-08:00","id":1497222,"title":"","content":"More ideas for organizations akin to the Rubber Band. Which of these should I write next?<br /> <br /> <u><b>Rubber Band Society [AA + FC]:</b></u> Fighters And Artists (Common Legacies: Universal Harmony, Uncrowned Kings, Perfected Adepts, Bearers Of The Sigil, Danse Diabolique, Pygmalian Society)<br /> <br /> <u><b>Corinthian Redeemers [SL + GOTV]:</b></u> Healers And Cultivators (Common Legacies: Phagocytes, Oneiric Physicians, Clavicularius, Dreamspeakers, Society Of Mithridates, Manus Dei)<br /> <br /> <u><b>Ars Futuri [SL + FC]:</b></u> Builders And Inventors (Common Legacies: Transhuman Engineers, Imagineers, Threnodists, Forge Masters, Anima Meccanica, Ego Programmers)<br /> <br /> <u><b>Anointed Eidolons [AA + GOTV]:</b></u> Paragons And Champions (Common Legacies: Knights Of Saint Martin, Knights Of Avalon, Choir Of Hashmallim, Agathos Kai Sophos, Karmic Equation, Brotherhood Of The Demon Wind)<br /> <br /> <u><b>Horizon Pilgrimage [MYS + AA]:</b></u> Travelers And Archivists (Common Legacies: Cryptologos, House Of Ariadne, Expeditious Explorers, Benthic Walkers, Walkers In Mists, Sphinxes)<br /> <br /> <u><b>Thaumaturgy Syndicate [SL + MYS]:</b></u> Teachers And Leaders (Common Legacies: Ductores Illuminans, Bene Ashmedai, Blank Badges, Keepers Of The Covenant, Sisterhood Of The Blessed, Thrice-Great)<br /> <br /> <u><b>Veracity Liberators [GOTV + FC]:</b></u> Tricksters And Chroniclers (Common Legacies: Stone Scribes, Illusionists Of Truth, The Fair Ones, Daoine, Eleventh Question, Skalds)<br /> <br /> <u><b>Apocryphal Locksmiths [MYS + GOTV]:</b></u> Linguists And Cryptographers (Common Legacies: Stone Scribes, Cryptologos, Ascended Adepts, Imagineers, Skalds, Sphinxes)<br /> <br /> <u><b>Note:</b></u> Some of these Legacies are fan-made, and authored by me and others. A few are only WIPs in my files right now. I'm currently very tired and unfocused, so I won't be providing elaborations or hyperlinks right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 11-29-2022, 02:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-15T15:10:35-08:00","id":1497226,"title":"","content":"My vote is for Ars Futuri, I love those kind of legacies, and a mystery cult based around them would be very interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-15T15:10:56-08:00","id":1497227,"title":"","content":"Corinthian Redeemers!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-15T15:36:46-08:00","id":1497232,"title":"","content":"Thaumaturgy Syndicate sounds delightfully ominous - &quot;Syndicate&quot; has such a negative connotation these days. My vote goes there!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-15T16:54:14-08:00","id":1497236,"title":"","content":"Very tough choice, all sound interesting. Horizon Pilgrimage, since I am curious to see more of the world of archeomancers. Anoited Eidolons are my second choice, to see their take on heroism amidst the cold war of the Awakened.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-29T00:36:19-08:00","id":1498276,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\"><u><b>Ars Futuri</b></u></span><br /> <br /> <b>[Flavor Text To Be Written]</b><br /> <br /> <b>Purpose:</b> Demonstrating and promoting the benefits of scientific inquiry and technological progress.<br /> <br /> <b>Relic:</b> An ancient computational device based on analogue principles, akin to the Antikythera Mechanism. It incorporates sophisticated alloys and &quot;circuitry&quot; composed of Perfected Metals and High Speech Runes, and it can be used as a +2 Tool Yantra for any spell related to the purview of this Mystery Cult.<br /> <br /> <b>Doctrine:</b> A combination of the ideologies of the Silver Ladder and the Free Council, mainly the precept of philanthropic empowerment and spiritual tuition of Sleepers, and the belief in the capacity of the scientific method and technological innovation to influence the Supernal Realms.<br /> <br /> <b>Common Legacies:</b> Transhuman Engineers, Imagineers, Threnodists, Forge Masters, Anima Meccanica, Ego Programmers.<br /> <br /> <b>Initiation Benefits</b><br /> \u25cf - A Specialty for Crafts, Science, Computers or equivalent Mental Skill reflecting something like Mechanical Engineering, High-Energy Physics or Programming.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf - Contacts (Inventors or Researchers).<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf - +1 Crafts, Science, Computers or equivalent Mental Skill.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf - Technopathy 3 or Omen Sensitivity.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf - Access to 3 dots in an Influence related to science or technology, which can be activated via Willpower instead of Essence on a 1 for 1 ratio. Their dice pool is based on the type of Influence, but it defaults to [Intelligence + Most Relevant Mental Skill]. They may also acquire Merits that enhance or alter their Influences by making Pacts and learning Thaumaturgy, as detailed in Summoners and Second Sight, respectively.<br /> <br /> Mages replace the benefit of the 4th level of Initiation with 3 Rotes related to science or technology. Instead of the benefit of the 5th level of Initiation, the Mage can achieve Exceptional Success with 3 Successes when he casts any spell related to science or technology, once per Chapter. This cannot be stacked with Rotes, but if stacked with a Praxis, the Mage can acquire 2 distinct benefits of Exceptional Success on spellcasting, such as Mana Refill and an Arcane Condition, but not two Arcane Conditions. Mages of the Ars Futuri often use this benefit to acquire Persistent Arcane Conditions with symbolically fitting advantages and disadvantages. Consult this <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S5lA00oP8kKrYW76B0bRVn-vYyy5Hl6aKQFtCakVPck/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><b>list of homebrewed Persistent Arcane Conditions</b></a> for examples. Mages may also pay Mana per Story to have temporary access to additional benefits within the Ars Futuri's purview, similarly to the Rubber Band Society.<br /> <br /> <b>[Plot Hooks To Be Written]</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 11-29-2022, 07:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}